  "id": "fb7ef457-3d87-4fc9-800d-71e7747c3627",
  "title": "ABot-World-0: Infinite Interactive World Rollout on a Single Desktop GPU",
  "summary": "ABot-World-0 presents a new approach to real-time, long-horizon closed-loop interaction with a video world model, leveraging multi-source data to learn controllable world dynamics. It offers a unified pipeline for agent-driven collection, training feedback, and efficient inference across different GPU configurations.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "ABot-World-0 streams 720P video at up to 16 FPS on a single NVIDIA RTX 5090 desktop GPU with 1.2s action-to-first-frame latency.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "It uses a lightweight VAE decoder, efficient attention, memory-aware scheduling, and low-bit DiT inference for deployment.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "ABot-World-0 demonstrates competitive controllability and coherent long-horizon world evolution in experiments on WorldRoamBench and extended interactive rollouts.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
